2:Tc91,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the weather in lahore today?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Current temperature in lahore is 38°C with clear sky. Check the live weather widget on this page for hourly updates, UV index, humidity, and wind speed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are today's prayer times in lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Today's prayer times in lahore: Fajr at 03:18, Maghrib at 19:08. All five prayer times are shown live on this page, calculated using the Karachi method. A full monthly timetable and Qibla compass are on the Prayer Times page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the gold rate in lahore today?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Gold rates in lahore are updated daily and shown in all karats (24K, 22K, 21K, 18K) in both grams and tolas. Check the Gold & Rates section on this page or visit the full Rates page for detailed charts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is lahore famous for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"lahore is famous for its Mughal-era monuments (Badshahi Mosque, Lahore Fort, Shalimar Gardens), its rich food culture (nihari, karahi, street food of Food Street), its literary and artistic heritage (Allama Iqbal, Faiz Ahmed Faiz), and its role as Pakistan's cultural capital. The city is also Pakistan's second-largest economic hub and home to top universities including LUMS and Punjab University."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the population of lahore in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"lahore's population in 2026 is estimated at over 13 million in the metropolitan area, making it Pakistan's second-largest city after Karachi. The city's population has grown rapidly due to rural-to-urban migration and a high birth rate, with growth projected to continue through 2040."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What language is spoken in lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The primary languages spoken in lahore are Punjabi (the mother tongue of the majority of residents) and Urdu (the national language used in education, government, and media). English is widely used in business, universities, and upscale neighbourhoods. Many residents are multilingual, switching between Punjabi, Urdu, and English in daily life."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the emergency number in lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In lahore, call 15 for Police, 1122 for Rescue/Ambulance (Rescue 1122 is one of Pakistan's best emergency services), and 16 for the Fire Brigade. The Edhi Foundation ambulance is reachable at 115. Women's helpline: 1043. All numbers are free to call from any mobile or landline."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the best time to visit lahore?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The best time to visit lahore is October to March when temperatures are pleasant (10°C–25°C), the air quality is better, and major cultural festivals take place. Avoid May–July when temperatures regularly exceed 40°C. The monsoon season (July–September) brings heavy rain and high humidity but also green parks and a vibrant street food atmosphere."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],"$L3","$L4","$L5","$L6"],null,"$L7"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mOntAhvblFrW_RuM8R868"}
