24:T41d,lahore's economy in June 2026 is one of the most dynamic in pakistan, contributing an estimated 13% of Pakistan's total GDP despite covering less than 1% of the country's land area. The city's economic engine runs on a diverse mix of manufacturing (textiles, leather goods, surgical instruments), services (banking, IT, retail), and the informal economy that employs millions across its 13 administrative towns. pakistan's GDP per capita currently stands at approximately USD 1,479, with annual inflation running at 13% — figures that have a direct impact on the daily purchasing power of lahore's residents. Unemployment (5%) masks a significant rate of underemployment, particularly among the city's large youth population. lahore's fastest-growing sectors include IT services, e-commerce, and food delivery — industries that are reshaping the employment landscape and creating new opportunities alongside traditional industries. For a full economic health score, sector breakdown, and decade-long growth charts, visit the Economy page for lahore.12:["$","section",null,{"id":"economy","className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"style":{"fontFamily":"Playfair Display, serif"},"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-[#01411C] mb-4","children":["📊 Economy of ","lahore"," — ","June"," ",2026]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#F5F3EE] rounded-xl p-4 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1","children":"GDP per Capita"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"font-mono font-bold text-[#01411C]","children":["$$","1,479"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#F5F3EE] rounded-xl p-4 text-center","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1","children":"Inflation"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"font-mono font-bold text-[#01411C]","children":"13%"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#F5F3EE] rounded-xl p-4 text-center"