 leading-relaxed text-sm","children":"Emergency contacts in lahore: Police (پولیس) can be reached at , Rescue/Ambulance at , and the Fire Brigade at . The Rescue 1122 service in lahore is one of the most professionally run emergency response services in Pakistan, with average response times of under 7 minutes across most of the city. The Edhi Foundation, reachable at 115, also operates ambulance services throughout lahore and is available 24/7. For women in distress, the Punjab Women Helpline is 1043. Child protection services can be reached at 1121. These numbers are available free of charge from any mobile or landline in lahore, and operators are available in Urdu, Punjabi, and English. In a medical emergency, heading to the nearest major hospital — Mayo Hospital, Services Hospital, or Jinnah Hospital — is advised; all three have 24-hour emergency departments. Keep these numbers saved in your phone before venturing out in lahore."}]]}]
